2026-06-14:03:20|f837d3549+patch4|/home/owner/qwen/Qwen3.5-4B-Q4_K_M-MTP.gguf|1.67t/s|9.90t/s|IME2-A100-FA-MTP-4B-prenorm|LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/home/owner/llama-smt/build/bin /home/owner/llama-smt/build/bin/llama-speculative-simple -m Qwen3.5-4B-Q4_K_M-MTP.gguf --spec-type draft-mtp --spec-draft-n-max 4 --no-spec-draft-backend-sampling -t 8 --no-mmap -fa 1 -n 60 --temp 0 -p "Write a short poem about a robot."|Patch 4 routes Qwen3.5 to pre-output-norm tap via llama_model_mtp_uses_nextn=false. Dispatch log confirms "mtp tap: pre_norm (target arch dictates)". accept=1.293% (3/232) - WORSE than patch 2's broken-nextn path (2.2%). Hypothesis disproven: pre_norm is not what the trained gguf expects. Upstream commit 166fe2949 chose POST-output-norm for Qwen3.5 MTP. Fork currently exposes neither a post-output-norm tap for Qwen3.5 nor a working nextn for Qwen3.5. Patch 5 must add a post-output-norm tap to qwen35.cpp/qwen35moe.cpp trunk+MTP graphs.
