2026-06-14:06:30|f837d3549+patch6ab|/home/owner/models/Qwen3.5-4B-Q4_K_M-MTP.gguf|4.72t/s|10.33t/s|IME2-A100-FA-MTP-4B-postnorm-hookwired|LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/home/owner/llama-smt/build/bin /home/owner/llama-smt/build/bin/llama-speculative-simple -m /home/owner/models/Qwen3.5-4B-Q4_K_M-MTP.gguf --spec-type draft-mtp --spec-draft-n-max 4 --no-spec-draft-backend-sampling -t 8 --no-mmap -fa 1 -n 60 --temp 0 -p "Write a short poem about a robot."|MAJOR WIN. Patch 6a's L2 probes revealed input-to-mtp was always L2=0.000 (zero-vector h input). Root cause: speculative-simple bypassed common_speculative_process(), so MTP impl's process() hook was never called → pending_h never populated. Patch 6b replaces direct llama_decode(ctx_dft, batch_tgt) with common_speculative_process(spec, batch_tgt). Result: accept=47.619% (40/84), tg=4.72 t/s (~10x accept jump, ~2.5x tg jump vs patch 5). Probe sequence confirms: process/trunk-row0 L2=153.7 → process/verify-row0 L2=153.7 → next draft/input-to-mtp L2=153.7 (clean propagation). MTP-output L2~173 vs naive ~50 expected, but RMSNorm post-norm with learned gamma typically scales 2-4x so this is reasonable. NOTE: still below 7 t/s non-MTP baseline; the per-draft MTP graph cost dominates. Model relocated to /home/owner/models/.
2026-06-14:07:15|f837d3549+patch6c|/home/owner/models/Qwen3.5-4B-Q4_K_M-MTP.gguf|4.585t/s|10.68t/s|IME2-A100-FA-MTP-4B-postnorm-warmup|LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/home/owner/llama-smt/build/bin /home/owner/llama-smt/build/bin/llama-speculative-simple -m /home/owner/models/Qwen3.5-4B-Q4_K_M-MTP.gguf --spec-type draft-mtp --spec-draft-n-max 4 --no-spec-draft-backend-sampling -t 8 --no-mmap -fa 1 -n 60 --temp 0 -p "Write a short poem about a robot."|Patch 6c adds pre-loop warmup: decode id_last on ctx_tgt + common_speculative_process(spec, warmup) to seed pending_h with h(id_last), then KV rollback on ctx_tgt+ctx_dft so iter 1 re-decodes id_last cleanly. CORRECTNESS WIN: first-iter probe now shows draft/input-to-mtp L2=153.791 (was 0.000 in 6a/6b first-iter). Perf: accept=44.318% (39/88), tg=4.585 t/s — within run-to-run noise of 6b (47.6%, 4.72 t/s); the recovered cycle is just 1 of ~22 over a 60-token run. Probe trace confirms iter 1 now executes 4 full draft steps (was 0 useful steps before) with proper h propagation. Still ~33% below non-MTP 7 t/s baseline.
